Program 9: Function to check prime number
A prime number has exactly two factors: 1 and itself.
public class PrimeNumber {

    boolean isPrime(int number) {

        if (number <= 1) {
            return false;
        }

        for (int i = 2; i < number; i++) {

            if (number % i == 0) {
                return false;
            }
        }

        return true;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        PrimeNumber obj = new PrimeNumber();

        boolean result = obj.isPrime(13);

        if (result) {
            System.out.println("Prime Number");
        } else {
            System.out.println("Not Prime Number");
        }
    }
}
Output
Prime Number
Explanation
•	The method checks divisibility from 2 to number - 1.
•	If divisible by any number, it returns false.
•	Otherwise, it returns true.
Types of functions in Java
Type	Description
No parameters, no return	Performs a task without input/output value.
Parameters, no return	Takes input but does not return a value.
No parameters, return	Returns a value without taking input.
Parameters, return	Takes input and returns a value.
Key points to remember
•	A function is declared with a return type, method name, and parameters.
•	void means the method does not return any value.
•	return sends a value back to the calling method.
•	Functions improve code reusability and program organization.
